        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_massive_cluster_is_born_(potm2401a).tiff"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 4.8,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.804,
      "end": 11.499,
      "text": "Our familiar Orion Nebula is close, but jump 160,000 light-years into deep space.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "The Orion Nebula* (eso1103a).tiff",
        "credit": "ESO/Igor Chekalin",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Orion_Nebula*_(eso1103a).tiff"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.8,
          "end": 8.167,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 8.167,
          "end": 11.5,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 11.499,
      "end": 17.519,
      "text": "There, inside the Large Magellanic Cloud galaxy, lies the colossal Tarantula Nebula.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Cloudy with a Chance of Star Formation (iotw2547a).jpg",
        "credit": "NOIRLab/NSF/AURA/P. Hor\u00e1lek (Institute of Physics in Opava)",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cloudy_with_a_Chance_of_Star_Formation_(iotw2547a).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 11.5,
          "end": 13.7,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 13.7,
          "end": 17.533,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 17.519,
      "end": 24.214,
      "text": "Spanning roughly 1,000 light-years across, it is the most energetic star factory in our Local Group.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "The Tarantula Nebula - Flickr - William Ostling.png",
        "credit": "William Ostling",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Tarantula_Nebula_-_Flickr_-_William_Ostling.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 17.533,
          "end": 20.933,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 20.933,
          "end": 24.2,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 24.214,
      "end": 30.734,
      "text": "At its heart, cluster R136 contains some of the most massive stars ever discovered.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Grand star-forming region R136 in NGC 2070 (visible and ultraviolet, captured by the Hubble Space Telescope).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA, ESA, F. Paresce (INAF-IASF, Bologna, Italy), R. O'Connell (University of Virginia, Charlottesville), and the Wide Field Camera 3 Science Oversight Committee",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grand_star-forming_region_R136_in_NGC_2070_(visible_and_ultraviolet,_captured_by_the_Hubble_Space_Telescope).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 24.2,
          "end": 28.033,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 28.033,
          "end": 30.733,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 30.734,
      "end": 36.779,
      "text": "This dense star cluster unleashes a torrent of radiation that powers the entire cloud.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "NASA Telescopes Create Colorful 'Craft' From Nearby Nebula (Tarantula Nebula Composite Crop).jpg",
        "credit": "X-ray: NASA/CXC/Ohio State Univ./J. Rodriguez et al; Infrared: NASA/ESA/CSA/STScI; Optical: NASA/ESA/STScI; Image Processing: NASA/CXC/SAO/P. Edmonds",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NASA_Telescopes_Create_Colorful_%27Craft%27_From_Nearby_Nebula_(Tarantula_Nebula_Composite_Crop).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 30.733,
          "end": 36.767,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 36.779,
      "end": 42.979,
      "text": "If moved to Orion's distance, this glowing giant would cover forty percent of the night sky.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Orion Nebula (Messier 42).jpg",
        "credit": "ESO/J. Emerson/VISTA.",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Orion_Nebula_(Messier_42).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 36.767,
          "end": 42.967,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 42.979,
      "end": 47.84,
      "text": "Its overwhelming light would make every object at midnight cast visible shadows.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "A massive cluster is born (potm2401a).tiff",
